  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered or otherwise leaves the stack without resolving.",
      "oracle_id": "01a7e0ce-c98f-4cf2-aba3-360aa0a9b9a7",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Bedlam Reveler\u2019s first ability can\u2019t reduce the {R}{R} in its cost.",
      "oracle_id": "01a7e0ce-c98f-4cf2-aba3-360aa0a9b9a7",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you have no cards in hand when Bedlam Reveler\u2019s enters ability resolves, you just draw three cards.",
      "oracle_id": "01a7e0ce-c98f-4cf2-aba3-360aa0a9b9a7",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you\u2019re paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions (such as that of Bedlam Reveler\u2019s first ability). The mana value of the spell is determined by only its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast that spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "01a7e0ce-c98f-4cf2-aba3-360aa0a9b9a7",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you have no cards in hand when Dangerous Wager resolves, you\u2019ll simply draw two cards.",
      "oracle_id": "7e0d60d7-cb27-4e45-80d4-c29aef5d56b6",
      "published_at": "2012-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of X is determined only as Peer Past the Veil resolves, after you discard your hand. Since Peer Past the Veil is still on the stack while it's resolving, it won't count itself.",
      "oracle_id": "8fb7ad08-9bb2-49f1-8ed0-8cc8abca4fe0",
      "published_at": "2024-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Change of Fortune counts cards you discarded this turn for any reason, not just cards you discarded as part of the resolution of this effect.",
      "oracle_id": "925feb7e-7876-430b-b95a-92b236a2e409",
      "published_at": "2021-11-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a player has fewer than seven cards in their library, that player loses the game after Dragon Mage's triggered ability resolves. If each player loses the game this way, the game's a draw.",
      "oracle_id": "eab71e4e-27c3-4c41-b95f-259c1d14b97a",
      "published_at": "2019-07-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a player has fewer than seven cards in their library, that player loses the game after Dragon Mage's triggered ability resolves. If each player loses the game this way, the game's a draw.",
      "oracle_id": "eab71e4e-27c3-4c41-b95f-259c1d14b97a",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as the value of X when casting it without paying its mana cost.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an attacking creature has multiple evasion abilities, such as shadow and flying, a creature can block it only if that creature satisfies all of the appropriate evasion abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you cast a card this way, you may not cast it for any other alternative costs it has, but you may pay for additional costs, such as kicker costs. If the spell requires an additional cost, you must pay that cost.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If your opponent discards a card while you control Dauthi Voidwalker, abilities that function when that card is discarded still work, even though that card never reaches that player's graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of the discarded card can find that card in exile.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Playing a card with Dauthi Voidwalker's last ability is still subject to normal timing restrictions.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tokens still die while Dauthi Voidwalker is on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While Dauthi Voidwalker is on the battlefield, nontoken creatures your opponents control won't die. They'll be exiled instead. Abilities that would trigger when those creatures die won't trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
